radv/ps5: a buffer or vertex-buffer descriptor at an address no PS5 mapping can have is written empty (after lead-mesh-17)

The console grants no address at or above 1 TiB and a GPU address is the CPU's (radv_ps5_bo.c), so a descriptor whose
address is up there is garbage. Ocarina of Time on Longshot, 2026-11-18 18:5x: a vertex shader's fetch (program
79323d04f98f23d3's, its first tbuffer loads) read 0x788001c0000 and the GPU fault ended the title; an earlier one read 0.
radv_write_vertex_descriptor and radv_write_buffer_descriptor (vkUpdateDescriptorSets, templates, push descriptors) write
such a descriptor empty, which reads zeros under robust access, and say so: up to 32 lines, the address, range, binding
or descriptor type, and the graphics pipeline (lead-mesh-17's log names its program).

